---An instance-attached disk resource.
---@class gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.Disk
---@field autoDelete? boolean Indicates whether the disk will be auto-deleted when the instance is deleted (but not when the disk is detached from the instance).
---@field deviceName? string Indicates a unique device name of your choice that is reflected into the `/dev/disk/by-id/google-*` tree of a Linux operating system running within the instance. This name can be used to reference the device for mounting, resizing, and so on, from within the instance. If not specified, the server chooses a default device name to apply to this disk, in the form persistent-disk-x, where x is a number assigned by Google Compute Engine.This field is only applicable for persistent disks.
---@field type? string Indicates the type of the disk, either `SCRATCH` or `PERSISTENT`. Valid values: * `PERSISTENT` * `SCRATCH`
---@field interface? string Indicates the disk interface to use for attaching this disk, which is either SCSI or NVME. The default is SCSI. Persistent disks must always use SCSI and the request will fail if you attempt to attach a persistent disk in any other format than SCSI. Local SSDs can use either NVME or SCSI. For performance characteristics of SCSI over NVMe, see Local SSD performance. Valid values: * `NVME` * `SCSI`
---@field licenses? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.StringList A list of publicly visible licenses. Reserved for Google's use. A License represents billing and aggregate usage data for public and marketplace images.
---@field kind? string Type of the resource. Always compute#attachedDisk for attached disks.
---@field diskSizeGb? string Indicates the size of the disk in base-2 GB.
---@field mode? string The mode in which to attach this disk, either `READ_WRITE` or `READ_ONLY`. If not specified, the default is to attach the disk in `READ_WRITE` mode. Valid values: * `READ_ONLY` * `READ_WRITE`
---@field guestOsFeatures? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.GuestOsFeatureList Indicates a list of features to enable on the guest operating system. Applicable only for bootable images. Read Enabling guest operating system features to see a list of available options.
---@field boot? boolean Indicates that this is a boot disk. The virtual machine will use the first partition of the disk for its root filesystem.
---@field source? string Indicates a valid partial or full URL to an existing Persistent Disk resource.
---@field index? string A zero-based index to this disk, where 0 is reserved for the boot disk. If you have many disks attached to an instance, each disk would have a unique index number.

