---The definition of a notebook instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.Instance
---@field customGpuDriverPath? string Specify a custom Cloud Storage path where the GPU driver is stored. If not specified, we'll automatically choose from official GPU drivers.
---@field migrated? boolean Output only. Bool indicating whether this notebook has been migrated to a Workbench Instance
---@field postStartupScript? string Path to a Bash script that automatically runs after a notebook instance fully boots up. The path must be a URL or Cloud Storage path (`gs://path-to-file/file-name`).
---@field dataDiskType? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.InstanceDataDiskTypeEnum Input only. The type of the data disk attached to this instance, defaults to standard persistent disk (`PD_STANDARD`).
---@field vmImage? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.VmImage Use a Compute Engine VM image to start the notebook instance.
---@field installGpuDriver? boolean Whether the end user authorizes Google Cloud to install GPU driver on this instance. If this field is empty or set to false, the GPU driver won't be installed. Only applicable to instances with GPUs.
---@field kmsKey? string Input only. The KMS key used to encrypt the disks, only applicable if disk_encryption is CMEK. Format: `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/keyRings/{key_ring_id}/cryptoKeys/{key_id}` Learn more about [using your own encryption keys](/kms/docs/quickstart).
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.StringMap Labels to apply to this instance. These can be later modified by the setLabels method.
---@field containerImage? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.ContainerImage Use a container image to start the notebook instance.
---@field machineType? string Required. The [Compute Engine machine type](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/machine-resource) of this instance.
---@field network? string The name of the VPC that this instance is in. Format: `projects/{project_id}/global/networks/{network_id}`
---@field noProxyAccess? boolean If true, the notebook instance will not register with the proxy.
---@field canIpForward? boolean Optional. Flag to enable ip forwarding or not, default false/off. https://cloud.google.com/vpc/docs/using-routes#canipforward
---@field createTime? string Output only. Instance creation time.
---@field serviceAccountScopes? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.StringList Optional. The URIs of service account scopes to be included in Compute Engine instances. If not specified, the following [scopes](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/access/service-accounts#accesscopesiam) are defined: - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/userinfo.email If not using default scopes, you need at least: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/compute
---@field nicType? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.InstanceNicTypeEnum Optional. The type of vNIC to be used on this interface. This may be gVNIC or VirtioNet.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Instance update time.
---@field proxyUri? string Output only. The proxy endpoint that is used to access the Jupyter notebook.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.StringMap Custom metadata to apply to this instance. For example, to specify a Cloud Storage bucket for automatic backup, you can use the `gcs-data-bucket` metadata tag. Format: `"--metadata=gcs-data-bucket=BUCKET"`.
---@field noRemoveDataDisk? boolean Input only. If true, the data disk will not be auto deleted when deleting the instance.
---@field creator? string Output only. Email address of entity that sent original CreateInstance request.
---@field instanceMigrationEligibility? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.InstanceMigrationEligibility Output only. Checks how feasible a migration from UmN to WbI is.
---@field disks? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.DiskList Output only. Attached disks to notebook instance.
---@field tags? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.StringList Optional. The Compute Engine network tags to add to runtime (see [Add network tags](https://cloud.google.com/vpc/docs/add-remove-network-tags)).
---@field acceleratorConfig? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.AcceleratorConfig The hardware accelerator used on this instance. If you use accelerators, make sure that your configuration has [enough vCPUs and memory to support the `machine_type` you have selected](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/gpus/#gpus-list).
---@field instanceOwners? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.StringList Input only. The owner of this instance after creation. Format: `alias@example.com` Currently supports one owner only. If not specified, all of the service account users of your VM instance's service account can use the instance.
---@field noPublicIp? boolean If true, no external IP will be assigned to this instance.
---@field reservationAffinity? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.ReservationAffinity Optional. The optional reservation affinity. Setting this field will apply the specified [Zonal Compute Reservation](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/reserving-zonal-resources) to this notebook instance.
---@field dataDiskSizeGb? string Input only. The size of the data disk in GB attached to this instance, up to a maximum of 64000 GB (64 TB). You can choose the size of the data disk based on how big your notebooks and data are. If not specified, this defaults to 100.
---@field name? string Output only. The name of this notebook instance. Format: `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/instances/{instance_id}`
---@field upgradeHistory? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.UpgradeHistoryEntryList The upgrade history of this instance.
---@field subnet? string The name of the subnet that this instance is in. Format: `projects/{project_id}/regions/{region}/subnetworks/{subnetwork_id}`
---@field state? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.InstanceStateEnum Output only. The state of this instance.
---@field serviceAccount? string The service account on this instance, giving access to other Google Cloud services. You can use any service account within the same project, but you must have the service account user permission to use the instance. If not specified, the [Compute Engine default service account](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/access/service-accounts#default_service_account) is used.
---@field bootDiskSizeGb? string Input only. The size of the boot disk in GB attached to this instance, up to a maximum of 64000 GB (64 TB). The minimum recommended value is 100 GB. If not specified, this defaults to 100.
---@field shieldedInstanceConfig? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.ShieldedInstanceConfig Optional. Shielded VM configuration. [Images using supported Shielded VM features](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/modifying-shielded-vm).
---@field diskEncryption? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.InstanceDiskEncryptionEnum Input only. Disk encryption method used on the boot and data disks, defaults to GMEK.
---@field bootDiskType? gcp.unstable.notebooks_v1.InstanceBootDiskTypeEnum Input only. The type of the boot disk attached to this instance, defaults to standard persistent disk (`PD_STANDARD`).

